T("Reading","Reading: Terry Fox","Read about a Canadian hero","🏃","",
 ["In a biography, follow the order of events.", "Look for the person's reason: why did they act?", "The final sentence often explains why the person is remembered."],
 ["Why did Terry Fox lose his leg?|He had cancer|He was in a car accident|He was injured while running|He was born without it", "Why did he decide to run across Canada?|To raise money for cancer research|To set a world record|To win a race|To become famous", "Where did the Marathon of Hope begin?|St. John's, Newfoundland|Thunder Bay, Ontario|Vancouver, British Columbia|Ottawa, Ontario", "About how far did he run each day?|About a marathon|About one kilometre|About 100 kilometres|About 500 metres", "Why did he have to stop?|The cancer had returned|He ran out of money|Winter arrived|He reached the ocean", "How many days did he run?|143|43|365|80", "Why is Terry Fox still remembered?|Runs in his name still raise money for research|He finished the run across Canada|He became a doctor|He wrote many books", "What quality does the text show most?|Determination|Laziness|Fear|Greed"],"","Terry Fox was eighteen when he lost his right leg to cancer. In hospital he saw how much other patients suffered, and he decided to run across Canada to raise money for research. He began his Marathon of Hope in April 1980 in St. John's, Newfoundland, running about a marathon every day on one real leg and one artificial one. After 143 days and more than 5,000 kilometres, the cancer returned and he had to stop near Thunder Bay, Ontario. Terry died the following year, but runs held in his name still raise money around the world.");
T("Reading","Reading: Plastic in the ocean","Read an argument and answer","🌊","",
 ["This writer wants to persuade you.", "A fact can be checked. An opinion is what someone thinks or believes.", "Notice how the writer answers people who disagree."],
 ["What does the writer want towns to do?|Ban single-use plastic bags|Build more factories|Stop fishing|Clean every beach daily", "Which sentence is a fact from the text?|A plastic bag can take hundreds of years to break down.|Every town should ban plastic bags.|A small change is a fair price.|Cloth bags are the best bags.", "Which sentence is the writer's opinion?|Every town should ban single-use plastic bags.|Millions of tonnes of plastic end up in the ocean.|Turtles sometimes mistake bags for jellyfish.|Plastic takes a long time to break down.", "Why are plastic bags dangerous to sea turtles?|Turtles can mistake them for food|They make the water too warm|They block the sunlight|They are too heavy", "What reasons does the writer give for cloth bags?|Easy to carry, long-lasting and cheap|Pretty, light and new|Free, large and waterproof|Strong, heavy and rare", "What do people who disagree say?|Bans are inconvenient|Plastic is healthy|Turtles like plastic|Cloth bags do not exist", "What is the purpose of this text?|To persuade|To entertain with a story|To give instructions|To describe a place"],"","Every year, millions of tonnes of plastic end up in the ocean. A plastic bag can take hundreds of years to break down, and sea turtles sometimes mistake bags for the jellyfish they eat. I believe every town should ban single-use plastic bags. Cloth bags are easy to carry, they last for years, and they cost very little. Some people say bans are inconvenient, but a small change in our habits is a fair price for cleaner seas.");
T("Spelling","Words that get mixed up","Affect or effect? Lose or loose?","⚖","Which word fits?",
 ["Some pairs of words sound alike but mean different things.", "Affect is usually an action. Effect is usually a thing.", "Lose means to misplace. Loose means not tight."],
 ["The rain will ___ the game.|affect|effect", "The medicine had a good ___.|effect|affect", "Please ___ this small gift.|accept|except", "Everyone came ___ Omar.|except|accept", "Do not ___ your ticket.|lose|loose", "My tooth is ___.|loose|lose", "She is taller ___ her brother.|than|then", "We ate, and ___ we left.|then|than", "___ coat is this?|Whose|Who's", "___ coming to the party?|Who's|Whose", "The library is a ___ place.|quiet|quite", "For ___, we had ice cream.|dessert|desert", "I do not know ___ it will rain.|whether|weather"],"");
T("Words","Fact or opinion","Can it be checked, or is it a belief?","🧐","Is this a fact or an opinion?",
 ["A fact can be proved true or false.", "An opinion is what someone thinks, feels or believes.", "Words like best, should, beautiful and boring often signal an opinion."],
 ["Ottawa is the capital of Canada.|Fact|Opinion", "Hockey is the most exciting sport.|Opinion|Fact", "Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius.|Fact|Opinion", "Winter is the best season.|Opinion|Fact", "A triangle has three sides.|Fact|Opinion", "Everyone should learn to swim.|Opinion|Fact", "The Pacific is the largest ocean.|Fact|Opinion", "Broccoli tastes terrible.|Opinion|Fact", "There are seven days in a week.|Fact|Opinion", "Cats make better pets than dogs.|Opinion|Fact", "Spiders have eight legs.|Fact|Opinion", "Reading is more fun than television.|Opinion|Fact"],"");

